    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-22734",
      "problem": "Convert $\\dfrac{79}{6}$ into a repeated decimal using long division.",
      "worked_solution": "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n79 \\div 6\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, continuing until a repeating pattern of digits appears after the decimal point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152429/assets/8e7826cba40e56c8a841b78336a06f8352d7587b59ccf40d600e0d39a75fb473.svg)\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $6$'s:\n\n$$\n13.16\\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{79}{6} = 13.16\\ldots = 13.1\\overline{6}.\n$$",
